## 3. Conclusion
In summary, by harnessing the powerful coordination ability of multifunctional additives with perovskite, we have successfully fabricated highly out-of-plane oriented PSCs exhibiting en
hanced crystallinity. This innovative design effectively suppresses non-radiative recombination and enhances carrier transport efficiency. As a result, we achieved a remarkable maximum efficiency of \(25.66\%\) in our PSCs. Furthermore, the fabricated PSCs demonstrate exceptional environmental and operational stability,
which underscores their potential for applications. Overall, this study unveils the significant potential of the synergistic effects between crystallization regulation, crystal spatial orientation, and defect passivation for improving the efficiency, and stability of PSCs.
